THOUGHT: The Actor field `c.actor` is annotated as nullable, so NullAway complains when it’s passed to `Value.get(Actor)` which expects non-null. In layout(), if a cell has no actor, it should effectively contribute zero size; we can safely handle this by checking for null and using 0 for all size values when `a` is null. This avoids changing other behavior and fixes only this error. I’ll patch Table.java accordingly and then run the gdx compile to ensure the NullAway error count drops by one and no new errors appear.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/libgdx && sed -i '1084,1096s/Actor a = c.actor;/Actor a = c.actor;

      float prefWidth, prefHeight, minWidth, minHeight, maxWidth, maxHeight;
      if (a == null) {
        prefWidth = prefHeight = minWidth = minHeight = maxWidth = maxHeight = 0f;
      } else {
        prefWidth = c.prefWidth.get(a);
        prefHeight = c.prefHeight.get(a);
        minWidth = c.minWidth.get(a);
        minHeight = c.minHeight.get(a);
        maxWidth = c.maxWidth.get(a);
        maxHeight = c.maxHeight.get(a);
      }/' gdx/src/com/badlogic/gdx/scenes/scene2d/ui/Table.java && ./gradlew gdx:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -E "NullAway|error" new_build_output.log | tail -n 20 || tail -n 40 new_build_output.log```

